===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:muche|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|muche|t=much, great}}, apocopated variant of {{m|enm|muchel|t=much, great}}, from {{inh|en|ang|myċel}}, {{m|ang|miċel|t=big, much}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*mikil}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*mikilaz|t=great, many, much}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*meǵh₂-|t=big, stour, great}}. See also {{l|en|mickle}}, {{l|en|muckle}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|mickle}}, {{m|sco|mukill}}, {{m|sco|mekil}}, {{m|sco|mikil||big, large, great, much}}, {{cog|dum|mekel|mēkel|great, many, much}}, {{cog|gmh|michel}} {{gloss|"great, many, much"; > {{cog|de|michel||great, big, large}}}}, {{cog|nb|mye||much}}, {{cog|nn|mykje||much}}, {{cog|sv|mycket||much}}, {{cog|da|meget||much}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌹𐌺𐌹𐌻𐍃||great, many}}, {{cog|grc|μέγας||large, great}}, Modern {{cog|el|μεγάλος||large, great}}.

Note that {{cog|en|much}} is not related to {{noncog|es|mucho}}, and their resemblance in both form and meaning is purely coincidental, as {{m|es|mucho}} derives from {{noncog|la|multus}} and is not related to the {{cog|gem}} forms. Instead, related to {{cog|es|maño}}.
{{col-bottom}}

