====Usage notes====
* {{m|en||Much}} is now generally used with [[uncountable]] nouns. The equivalent used with [[countable]] nouns is {{m|en|many}}. In positive contexts, ''much'' is widely avoided: ''I have '''a lot of''' money'' instead of ''I have '''much''' money''. There are some exceptions to this, however: ''I have '''much''' hope for the future.''  A lot of these cases are emotive transitive verbs and nouns.  ''I have '''much''' need for a new assistant.''  In parallel, ''I need it very '''much'''.''
* Unlike many determiners, but like many adjectives, {{m|en||much}} is frequently modified by intensifying adverbs, as in “too much”, “very much”, “so much”, and so on. (The same is true of {{m|en||many}}.)

